course: dictionary
lesson: 11298
title: Yank: a sudden, hard pull
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words show how something is done, not just what it is. «Yank» is one of them. Read this sentence: «Maddie grabbed both of Chloe's long plaits and yanked.» Grabbed and then yanked tells you the pull came quickly and roughly. So to yank means to pull something suddenly and hard.
explain: Look at another clue: «You should pull a plug out by holding the plug itself, not by yanking the cord, because yanking can damage the wires and break their plastic cover.» Pulling is the everyday action, but yanking is a fast, rough pull that can cause harm. Check your meaning by swapping it in: "pulling the cord suddenly and hard can damage the wires" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: A yank can also be a noun, meaning one quick, strong pull. Kai was «being yanked out of» his match, which means he was pulled away from it suddenly, not because he chose to leave. A capital Y, «Yank», is a different word. It is an informal name for a person from the USA, and some people think it is rude, so think before you use it.
fact: To yank means to pull something suddenly and hard.
fact: A yank is one quick, strong pull.
fact: Yanking is often done in a hurry, in anger or in an emergency.
fact: «Yank» with a capital Y is an informal word for a person from the USA, and some people find it rude.
fact: In science, a yank is a sudden pull force.
exercise: «Maddie grabbed both of Chloe's long plaits and yanked.» What did Maddie do? | Tied the plaits in a neat bow | Cut the plaits off with scissors | Let go of the plaits gently | *Pulled the plaits suddenly and hard
exercise: Why should you not yank the cord when you pull a plug out? | Because the plug gets too heavy to hold | *Because yanking can damage the wires and break their plastic cover | Because cords are always too short | Because it makes the plug shine
exercise: Which word means one quick, strong pull? | A whisper | A plug | *A yank | A cousin
test: In «being yanked out of it», what does yanked mean? | Carefully helped to finish | Painted over in bright colours | Hugged tightly | *Pulled away suddenly, often without choosing to go
test: «Evie was yanking another girl's hair at a birthday party.» What is Evie doing? | Dyeing the hair red | *Pulling the hair suddenly and hard | Brushing the hair gently | Singing a song to the hair
exam: In «Yank» with a capital Y, what does the word mean? | A type of plug for the wall | A loud noise in the street | A sudden, hard pull | *An informal name for a person from the USA
